output_text:
{
  "decline_reason": "I cannot determine whether your particular application requires a colour limitation; I can explain the practice recorded in the supplied Manual passages.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not establish that always using a barcode in green and blue, by itself, requires a colour limitation.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual says a mark consisting entirely of a simple barcode is unlikely to be prima facie capable of distinguishing.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part22/25/25/8",
          "quote": "As such a trade mark which consists entirely of a simple barcode is unlikely to be prima facie capable of distinguishing."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a mark merely used in particular colours, the Manual identifies colour limitation as a possible basis for acceptance where evidence of use establishes capacity to distinguish when used in those colours.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "This situation is most likely to occur when a trade mark which is lacking in inherent adaptation to distinguish is shown through evidence of use to be capable of distinguishing when used in particular colours. Acceptance for registration may then be allowed on the basis of a limitation to colour."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If an applicant chooses to limit to colour during examination, the Manual specifies the following endorsement, with the relevant colours inserted.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "Registration of this trade mark is limited to the colours ____________, ________ and _________ as shown in the representation of the trade mark attached to the application form."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "If an applicant chooses to limit to colour during examination, this same form of endorsement would be the appropriate one."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual treats wording that the mark is limited to green and blue as a colour limitation, rather than a claim to rights in those colours themselves.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "In those cases, the following descriptions will be taken as an indication of a restriction or limitation to a specific colour or colours:"
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "“The trade mark is limited to the colours green and blue as shown in the representation attached to the application form.”"
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/3/3/5/3~1",
          "quote": "It should be noted that this does not imply a claim to rights in the colour or colours themselves, but is a limitation on the rights of registration under section 70 of the Act."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "By contrast, the Manual does not treat merely saying that the mark is represented in green and blue as a colour limitation.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part21/4/4/1~2",
          "quote": "Descriptions for COLOURED trade marks which are allowable but will not be considered to be indicative of a restriction or limitation to colour"
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part21/4/4/1~2",
          "quote": "“The trade mark is represented in the colours green and blue.”"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    }
  ],
